# Layout — footer pegado al bottom + scroll del documento

## Never regress

- Short content (Contact Resume / Languages mobile): footer must stay at viewport bottom; no scrollable void above it.
- Short galleries (few images): no internal Tab scroll; no empty scrollable gallery area.

## Required pattern

- `main`: `flex flex-col min-h-screen`.
- `LayoutChrome`: page shell `flex flex-1 flex-col min-h-0`; children wrapper **without** `flex-1`.
- `Footer`: `mt-auto shrink-0` (spacing via `pt-[32px] md:pt-[64px]`).
- `Tab` `bodyClasses`: `overflow-visible` (project + contact).
- `WorkLayoutClient`: no `min-h-screen` on root.
- Contact page/Tab: natural height, no `flex-1 basis-0` chain on mobile.

## Do not

- `flex-1` / `basis-0` on Tab or route wrappers to “fill viewport” when content is document-scrolled.
- `overflow-y-auto` on Tab body for gallery/contact (creates internal scroll trap).
- Duplicate `min-h-screen` on work layout when `main` already has it.
- `min-h-dvh` on `body`/`main` or single-root `LayoutChrome` wrapper (regresión: footer invisible).

Full spec: `CLAUDE.md` §13.1
